<details>

<summary>Original prompt</summary>

> # PR 001 – Add Health Endpoint and Deterministic Readiness Logging
> 
> ## Problem
> The backend doesn't emit a clear "ready" message, and the setup wizard gets false "Backend Server Not Reachable" errors because there's no simple health check endpoint.
> 
> ## Solution
> 
> ### 1. Backend: Add `/healthz/simple` Endpoint
> **File: `Aura.Api/Program.cs`**
> 
> Add before `app.Run()`:
> ```csharp
> // Simple health endpoint (no dependencies)
> app.MapGet("/healthz/simple", () => Results.Ok(new
> {
>     status = "ok",
>     service = "Aura.Api",
>     version = typeof(Program).Assembly.GetName().Version?.ToString() ?? "unknown",
>     timestampUtc = DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("o")
> }));
> 
> // Deterministic startup message
> var lifetime = app.Services.GetRequiredService<IHostApplicationLifetime>();
> lifetime.ApplicationStarted.Register(() =>
> {
>     var logger = app.Services.GetRequiredService<ILogger<Program>>();
>     var addresses = app.Urls.Count > 0 ? string.Join(", ", app.Urls) : "configured URLs";
>     logger.LogInformation("Application started. Press Ctrl+C to shut down. Listening on: {Addresses}", addresses);
> });
> ```
> 
> ### 2. Frontend: Add Backend Ping to Setup Wizard
> **File: `Aura.Web/src/services/api/setupApi.ts`**
> 
> Add method:
> ```typescript
> async pingBackend(): Promise<{ ok: boolean; details?: string }> {
>   const config: ExtendedAxiosRequestConfig = { _skipCircuitBreaker: true };
>   try {
>     const response = await apiClient.get('/healthz/simple', config);
>     return { ok: response.status === 200, details: response.statusText };
>   } catch (error: any) {
>     return { ok: false, details: error?.message ?? 'Unknown error' };
>   }
> }
> ```
> 
> ### 3. Update Wizard to Ping Before FFmpeg Check
> **File: `Aura.Web/src/pages/Onboarding/FirstRunWizard.tsx`**
> 
> Before showing "Backend Server Not Reachable", retry with exponential backoff:
> ```typescript
> // In useEffect for step 2
> const checkBackendAndFFmpeg = async () => {
>   for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
>     const ping = await setupApi.pingBackend();
>     if (ping.ok) {
>       // Backend is up, check FFmpeg
>       setFfmpegRefreshSignal(prev => prev + 1);
>       return;
>     }
>     await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1000 * (i + 1)));
>   }
>   // Show backend not reachable error with instructions
> };
> ```
> 
> ## Testing
> - Start app without backend → See clear error with instructions
> - Start backend (`dotnet run --project Aura.Api`) → See "Application started. Press Ctrl+C to shut down." in console
> - Wizard Step 2 → FFmpeg check succeeds automatically
> - Hit `/healthz/simple` in browser → Get JSON response
> 
> ## Can Run in Parallel: **YES**


</details>



